## 1. Bow Turns Before Chute Six

**Story & Context:** The debut runs at 122 BPM. Theo opens with one compact kick on every quarter note, clipped clap on two and four, and a one-note acid bass pulse. Amina sustains a low goje pitch across two beats in DRAW, reverses into RETURN without changing finger position, then releases before beginning again. The bow reversal lands just before the electronic clap, creating a rasping pre-transient without any sample replacement. Zainab plays one prepared-clavichord fifth only after every second RELEASE. Idris replaces one programmed rim every four bars with a dry calabash slap. Martha enters only after Theo mutes the acid bass for eight bars. In the final section, Amina increases bow pressure but not pitch range; the track becomes harsher without adding notes.

