## 2. Dust Reading Holds While the Bow Changes

**Story & Context:** At 126 BPM, Theo uses the EP’s most insistent jack pattern but keeps the acid bass fixed to one root for nearly two minutes. Amina alternates long DRAW and RETURN strokes on the same pitch, gradually changing pressure so one direction sounds smooth and the other increasingly coarse. Zainab adds clipped minor-seventh dyads every eight bars. Idris uses fingertip calabash taps only when hats disappear. Martha contributes short plunger-muted fourths in the gaps between acid phrases. The central break removes kick and bass for four bars but leaves bow and calabash untouched, revealing that the groove remains legible through friction alone.

