## 3. Sluice Gate Closes on the Release

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 118 BPM and begins with minimal drums: kick, one shuffled hat, and no clap. Amina plays higher goje notes with long slides into a fixed tonic, then releases bow pressure completely at the end of each phrase. Theo places the acid bass only after those RELEASE points, creating a delayed low-frequency answer without direct triggering. Zainab plays isolated clavichord octaves, Idris uses low calabash palm hits every second phrase, and Martha holds one muted bass-trombone fundamental beneath the final third. During the last minute, electronic elements disappear one at a time. The final sound is a goje RETURN stroke ending in a completely dry RELEASE, followed by the mechanical clunk of the old sluice gate closing in the room.

